<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Edzná</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 900 CE (approx.) · capital Edzná</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maya city in western Campeche known for its five-storey palace pyramid and an extensive system of canals and reservoirs.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Edzná occupied a flood-prone valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a>. It was settled in the Preclassic, when inhabitants dug a large network of canals and a moat, and became an important centre in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-classic-period">Late Classic</a> from about 600 CE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its Great Acropolis carries the Building of the Five Storeys, combining a pyramid and palace rooms on each level. The city's architecture blends southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peten">Petén</a> styles with the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puuc">Puuc</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chenes">Chenes</a> styles of the north. Hieroglyphic stairways and stelae record its rulers, though their history is only partly understood. Water management supported farming in the valley through the dry season.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Monument building at Edzná ended around 900 CE, and the city declined, though some Postclassic occupation continued. It is now a protected archaeological site in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.64%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Edzná</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Edzna</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=750&amp;focus=edzna" aria-label="Edzná on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2243 1452 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Edzná lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2563 1708h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2563 1708h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=750&amp;focus=edzna">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

